  "Number": 8,
  "Question": "If \\(\\frac ba=2\\) and \\(\\frac cb=3,\\) what is the ratio of \\(a+b\\) to \\(b+c?\\)",
  "Question Type": "text",
  "Choices": {
    "A": "\\(\\frac13\\)",
    "B": "\\(\\frac38\\)",
    "C": "\\(\\frac35\\)",
    "D": "\\(\\frac23\\)",
    "E": "\\(\\frac34\\)"
  },
  "Choices Type": "text",
  "Correct Answer": "B",
  "Solution": "Expressing all three quantities in terms of \\(a\\) lets us compare the two sums directly. The given ratios imply \\(b=2a\\) and \\(c=3b=6a\\). Therefore\n\\[\n\\frac{a+b}{b+c}\n=\\frac{a+2a}{2a+6a}\n=\\frac{3a}{8a}\n=\\frac38.\n\\]\nThe original ratios require \\(a\\ne0\\), so \\(8a\\ne0\\) and the cancellation is valid. The answer is \\(\\frac38\\), choice B.",
